Explanation: These assert statements are relevant to the comment "@@@ some account of "frm" has more money than "amnt"". This comment states that at least one of "frm"'s accounts should have enough money (more than or equal to "amnt") to permit the transfer. The code snippet verifies this condition by checking if any of "frm"'s accounts (`frm.accounts`) has enough money (`acnt.money >= amnt`) for the transfer. 

So, `any(acnt.money >= amnt for acnt in frm.accounts)` checks if there is at least one account in `frm.accounts` which has at least the "amnt" balance. If such an account exists then it signals that transfer can proceed, otherwise, it signals that there is insufficient balance and thus the transfer should not happen.
