Also, the function `transfer` can return more than just True or False. It can be modified to return a specific error message if the transfer is not possible due to insufficient funds. Here it is:

```py
def transfer(frm, to, amnt):
    """ attempts to transfers "amnt" money from "frm" to "to". Returns a message indicating the transfer status. """

    #@@@ some account of "frm" has more than or equal money than "amnt"
    for acnt in frm.accounts:
        if (acnt.money >= amnt):
            acnt.money -= amnt
            to.accounts[0].money += amnt
            return f"Transfer of {amnt} from {frm.name} to {to.name} is successful."

    return f"Insufficient funds in any account of {frm.name}. Transfer attempt for {amnt} failed."
